# The other arity of the SAME C symbol, in its own module.
#
# `printf` again, `<stdio.h>` again, a different value type. Two `extern`
# groups in two modules naming one symbol is not a collision: the probes
# are mangled per module (panel 053), and the call goes through the
# header's own prototype, so C sees one function and Heroes sees two
# bindings. Both parameters say `lent` (panel 171): `printf` reads them
# while it runs and keeps neither.

extern "stdio.h"
    function printf(format: cstr lent, value: cstr lent) -> i32

# The wrapper takes two `str` and lends both inside itself, as `as_int.hero`
# says why.
function say(format: str, value: str) -> i32
    return printf(format: format.cstr(), value: value.cstr())
